many long-distance buses on major routes are night buses .
buses are much cheaper than trains , so students often use them .
buses are comfortable .
seats are big and they recline .
the bus has a toilet and makes rest stops .
taxis in Japan , as in other countries , run on meters .
the basic fare covers the first one point five to two kilometers . beyond that the fare goes up according to distance or time .
the basic fare varies depending on the size of the car .
between eleven at night and five in the morning , special high rates are applied .
taxis in Japan may be a little more expensive than in other countries .
but no tipping is necessary .
if you take a cab for a long distance , you don &apos;t have to pay for the return trip .
you don &apos;t have to pay extra for baggage , either .
the address numbers of Japanese houses are not much orderly .
